{"version":1,"name":"Ohio Grade 8 · 8.EE unit review","difficulty":"advanced","pace":"practice","questions":[{"text":"Write 5^(-1) × 5^(4) as one power of 5.","answers":["5^(2)","5^(5)","5^(4)","5^(3)"],"correct":3,"explanation":"For a common nonzero base, add the exponents.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.1","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"multiply-powers","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.1","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"multiply-powers","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Integer exponent properties","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Write 8^(0) ÷ 8^(5) as one power of 8.","answers":["8^(-6)","8^(-4)","8^(-5)","8^(-3)"],"correct":2,"explanation":"For a common nonzero base, subtract the exponents.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.1","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"divide-powers","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.1","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"divide-powers","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Integer exponent properties","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Find the nonnegative solution of x² = 64.","answers":["7","8","16","9"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A positive square has positive and negative square roots; the prompt asks for the nonnegative one.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.2","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"square-root","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.2","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"square-root","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Square and cube roots","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Solve x³ = 64.","answers":["5","3","4","8"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The real cube root is the number whose cube gives the right side.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.2","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"cube-root","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.2","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"cube-root","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Square and cube roots","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"How many times as large is 4 × 10^7 as 4 × 10^5?","answers":["200","101","99","100"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The matching coefficients cancel; subtract exponents to find the factor.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.3","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"larger-quantity","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.3","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"larger-quantity","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Compare powers-of-ten quantities","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"How many times does 5 × 10^3 fit into 5 × 10^4?","answers":["11","9","20","10"],"correct":3,"explanation":"The matching coefficients cancel; subtract exponents to find the factor.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.3","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"smaller-quantity","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.3","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"smaller-quantity","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Compare powers-of-ten quantities","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Compute (4 × 10^6) × (4 × 10^-2). Write normalized scientific notation.","answers":["1.6 × 10^6","1.7 × 10^5","1.6 × 10^5","1.6 × 10^4"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Combine coefficients and powers, then normalize the coefficient to at least 1 and below 10.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.4","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"scientific-product","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.4","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"scientific-product","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Scientific notation operations","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Compute (1 × 10^-4) + (4 × 10^-4). Write normalized scientific notation.","answers":["5 × 10^-5","5 × 10^-3","5 × 10^-4","6 × 10^-4"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Combine coefficients and powers, then normalize the coefficient to at least 1 and below 10.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.4","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"scientific-sum","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.4","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"scientific-sum","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Scientific notation operations","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"The graph shows distance versus time. What is its unit rate?","answers":["6","10","5","4"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Divide change in distance by change in time.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.5","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"graph-rate","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.5","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"coordinates","points":[[0,0],[1,5],[2,10],[3,15]],"segments":[[0,3]],"xLabel":"Time","yLabel":"Distance"},"format":"graph-rate","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Proportional graphs and slope","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Graph A is shown. Rule B is y = 5x. Which has the greater unit rate?","answers":["Graph A","Their unit rates are equal","Neither has a unit rate","Rule B"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Graph A has slope 2; Rule B has slope 5.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.5","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"compare-rates","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.5","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"coordinates","points":[[0,0],[1,2],[2,4],[3,6]],"segments":[[0,3]]},"format":"compare-rates","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Proportional graphs and slope","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"The points (1, 8), (3, 16), (5, 24) lie on one line. Find its constant slope.","answers":["3","8","4","5"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Similar slope triangles give the same rise/run on each segment.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.6","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"slope-from-points","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.6","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"coordinates","points":[[1,8],[3,16],[5,24]],"segments":[[0,2]]},"format":"slope-from-points","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Constant slope and line equations","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"A line has equation y = 7x + 10. What is its y-intercept?","answers":["9","10","11","20"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Set x = 0; the remaining constant is the intercept.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.6","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"initial-value","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.6","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"coordinates","points":[[1,11],[3,17],[5,23]],"segments":[[0,2]]},"format":"initial-value","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Constant slope and line equations","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Solve 5(x + 8) = 110.","answers":["14","13","28","15"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Distribute or divide first, preserving equality.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"distribute-and-solve","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.7","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"distribute-and-solve","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Linear equations and solution types","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"How many solutions does 5x + 8 = 5x + 9 have?","answers":["No solutions","Exactly two","Exactly one","Infinitely many"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Subtracting the same x terms leaves unequal constants.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"no-solution","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.EE.7","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"no-solution","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Linear equations and solution types","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"A student solves 3(x + 2) = 15 by writing 3x + 2 = 15. Which next step repairs the work?","answers":["Replace 3x with x + 3","Replace 3x + 2 with 3x + 6 before solving","Subtract 2 and stop","Keep 3x + 2 because distribution affects only x"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The factor 3 multiplies both x and 2. The correct solution is x = 3.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.EE.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"equation-error-analysis","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Expressions and equations","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=53","standardMeta":